<Layout>
	<Navigation />
	<h1>Khora</h1>


	<div>Software developers now have to explore and operate within an increasingly complex and constantly
		evolving design space, while having to deal with deploying new software releases faster. Khora is
		developing a research activity in software engineering to help developers in mastering their increasingly
		complex design space. To do so, Khora develops new scientific theories, approaches, and techniques
		related to exploratory programming, a development mode to try out, compare, explore different versions
		of software artifacts. Khora's research agenda implies working on: 1. domain-specific IDEs and
		digital twins to help developers master their development design space through novel exploratory
		programming features (augmented development environment); 2. large-scale, polyglot, AI-based,
		code analysis techniques to underpin exploratory programming (augmented code analysis). The
		application domains of Khora encompass software engineering with software artifacts (co-)evolution
		and optimization (e.g., reduce software energy consumption) and scientific computing to help scientists
		in their complex software development.
	</div>

	<div>Khora is a research group part of the IRISA laboratory (a mixed research unit grouping CNRS,
		University of Rennes, Inria, INSA Rennes), Rennes, France.</div>

</Layout>
